s7-6-p15 = prose (cons "(with universe levels and implicit parameters suppressed). `fleet-proc` requests the next environmental choice, computes `fleet-step`, and recurses for the specified number of steps. The complete fleet is therefore one process over its remaining environment. Message-passing actors and deterministic stream-process semantics are precedents for representing communicating agents as programs ([55](#ref-55), [56](#ref-56)); the fleet in this section is the particular defined program, not an additional primitive. Its nodes and their interactions are still individually programmable. Nothing about the language makes `FState`, `Pkt`, or `EnvS` distinguished primitive forms; they are names defined by this particular program." nil)
